Console frontend audit fixes: capture log
Date: 2026-09-01
Branch: fix/console-frontend-audit-2026-09-01
Issues: 1652 (blank notFound body), 1647 (Try in chat on non-chat models,
        Hidden badge), 1649 (invoice PDF 500 for an unknown id), 1653 (bidi
        control character rendering unescaped)

HOW THIS WAS CAPTURED

Console under test: the production build of this branch (next build, next
start) served on http://127.0.0.1:3199. Browser: Playwright chromium, viewport
1440x900 at 2x.

Upstreams: a local stub on http://127.0.0.1:4599 answering the two services the
console talks to, Supabase Auth (GET /auth/v1/user, POST /auth/v1/token) and
the control plane (viewer, catalog, API keys, usage events, profile, balance,
and the invoice PDF endpoint). Fixture rows below. No live tenant data, no live
credential, and no live database is involved: the session bearer is an unsigned
local JWT that only the stub accepts, so there is nothing here to redact and
nothing to revoke.

Why a stub rather than the deployed box: the demo box runs main, not this
branch, and the four defects are all console rendering defects whose inputs are
control-plane rows. Issue 1653 in particular needs a stored nickname carrying
U+202E, which is a row the fixture supplies rather than one written into a live
workspace.

FIXTURE ROWS THAT MATTER

  catalog (GET /api/v1/catalog/models), the badge arrays the migrations seed:
    hive-small              ["stable","chat","responses"]     lifecycle stable
    hive-fast               ["stable","chat","responses"]     lifecycle hidden
    hive-embedding-default  ["stable","embeddings"]           lifecycle stable
    hive-stt                ["voice","stt"]                   lifecycle stable
    hive-tts                ["voice","tts"]                   lifecycle stable

  api keys (GET /api/v1/accounts/current/api-keys):
    key-1 nickname "prod\u202Egnp.txt", the shape issue 1653 found stored live.
    Rendered without the fix, a browser reads that as "prodtxt.png".

PRE-FIX MEASUREMENT FOR ISSUE 1652 (this branch, before the change)

A probe route (async layout, async page, notFound() after an await) was built
into this app and served by next start, then removed. Next 16.3.2:

  GET /nfprobe            -> 404, 10038 bytes, <html id="__next_error__">,
                             body is <div hidden><!--$--><!--/$--></div>
  GET /does-not-exist-xyz -> 404, 15517 bytes, full styled body, no error shell

Repeated with a segment-scoped not-found.tsx beside the probe page: unchanged.
Repeated with an app/global-not-found.tsx plus experimental.globalNotFound:
unchanged for notFound(), while the unmatched URL did switch to it. Repeated on
next 16.3.4: unchanged. Repeated with a synchronous root layout: unchanged. So
the boundary file is not what selects that path, and the fix is to stop raising
notFound() on the two data-miss pages rather than to add another boundary.

